messages:
Tara: Heads-up  FinTechOrg wants a tight POC: websocket SDK streaming + function calls to pull KVPs, structured JSON (NDJSON) output for their ETL, short security answers, and a hosted vs Dedicated 2G pricing sketch. Can someone take the SDK + playbook?

Alex: Ill own the SDK examples. Quick detail: show websocket streaming with function_call:auto, auth via short-lived service token, and a small sketch for error/fallback to REST.

Mina: I can draft the security FAQ. They asked: are prompts stored, BYOK/KMS support, retention, subprocessors, and can function-call payloads be excluded from logs. I'll produce short canned answers and flag legal items.

Alex: Snippet (pseudo):
```js
// websocket streaming + function call
const ws = new RedwoodWS(URL, API_KEY);
ws.on('token', t=>process.stdout.write(t));
ws.on('function_call', async fc=>{
  // use service account token to call internal API
  const res = await fetch(`https://crm/_lookup/${fc.args.id}`, {headers:{Authorization:`Bearer ${SA_TOKEN}`}});
  ws.sendFunctionResult(fc.id, await res.json());
});
ws.send({model:'redwood-1-stream',stream:true,function_call:'auto',schema:{type:'object',properties:{type:{type:'string'}}}});
```

Alex: Include NDJSON output example and a tiny repair helper for truncated lines. Also a REST fallback curl example. Ill push a tiny repo and README.

infra-bot: POC env provisioned: id=fintech-poc-1801234567, url=https://console.redwood.example/poc/fintech-poc-1801234567

Mina: Security bullets: prompts not stored by default; BYOK for Private and enterprise-hosted KMS option; retention configurable up to 36 months; function-call payload logging can be disabled per route; subprocessors list in legal portal. Flagging BYOK SLA and subprocessors to legal.

Tara: Two asks before EOD: (1) Alex, one-pager with websocket + REST snippets + link to repo (2) Mina, short answers doc to paste into SFDC. Quick review 8:30am PT tomorrow.

Alex: Will do and include a small troubleshooting checklist (401 websocket auth, keepalive, partial JSON).

Mina: Looping legal after draft.

Tara: Thanks team :thumbsup:
